  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the speaker's perspective represented by the child",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the speaker (the woman) who is asking the man to see things from her point of view. The child in the image, looking out the window, serves as a visual metaphor for this speaker's perspective being ignored. The text 'I asked him to see things from my point of view' explicitly uses 'I' to anchor the projection onto the speaker, who is symbolized by the child. The user identifies with this speaker, projecting themselves onto the child's role as the overlooked viewpoint.",
